{
  "schema_version": 10,
  "name": "three stones",
  "description": "Chess in which either player has three stones and may, instead of moving, place one on any empty square. A stone never moves, is never captured and never leaves, so a placed stone is a square taken out of the game for good -- and there are only three of them, so the question is not whether to place one but when. Three is the difference between a game and none: in stones, where a player may place as many as they like, the board fills until nobody can move, while three a side leave a game that plays like chess with three well-timed walls in it.",
